@startuml ECU System Context – AUTOSAR IDS
!theme plain
skinparam defaultFontSize 11
skinparam actorStyle awesome

title ECU Deployment – System Context Diagram

' === External Actors ===
actor "OEM Diagnostic\nTester" as Tester
cloud "OEM Cloud\n(OTA Backend)" as Cloud
actor "Vehicle Driver" as Driver

' === Vehicle Network ===
package "Vehicle CAN Bus Network" as VehicleNet {
    node "CAN Bus\n(500 kbps)" as CAN_BUS #LightYellow {
    }

    node "Engine ECU" as ECU_ENG #LightCyan
    node "Transmission\nECU" as ECU_TRANS #LightCyan
    node "Body Control\nModule" as BCM #LightCyan
    node "OBD-II\nPort" as OBD #Orange
    node "Instrument\nCluster" as IC #LightCyan
}

' === Target ECU ===
node "Gateway ECU – IDS Host" as GW_ECU #LightGreen {
    component "AUTOSAR\nBSW Stack" as BSW
    component "IDS SWC\n(tiny-can-ids)" as IDS_SWC #PaleGreen
    component "DEM / DCM\n(Diagnostics)" as DIAG
    database "NvM\n(Event Log)" as NVM_DB
}

' === TCU for OTA relay ===
node "TCU / NAD\n(Connectivity)" as TCU #Plum {
    component "OTA Agent" as OTA
}

' === Data flows ===
ECU_ENG --> CAN_BUS : Engine\nframes
ECU_TRANS --> CAN_BUS : Gear/RPM\nframes
BCM --> CAN_BUS : Body\nframes
OBD --> CAN_BUS : <<potential\nattack vector>>

CAN_BUS --> GW_ECU : All CAN\nframes
BSW --> IDS_SWC : CAN PDUs\nvia COM/RTE
IDS_SWC --> DIAG : DTC on\nintrusion
IDS_SWC --> NVM_DB : Log\nevents
DIAG --> Tester : UDS response\n(DID 0xF1F0)

GW_ECU --> IC : IDS alert\n(warning lamp)
GW_ECU --> CAN_BUS : Filtered/blocked\nframes (gateway mode)

Cloud --> TCU : OTA model\nupdate package
TCU --> GW_ECU : Model update\nvia UDS/UCM

Driver --> IC : Observes\nalert

' === Attack scenarios ===
note right of OBD
  **Attack vectors monitored:**
  DoS (flood), Fuzzy (random),
  Gear spoofing, RPM spoofing
end note

note bottom of IDS_SWC
  **Classification modes:**
  • Binary: normal vs attack
  • Multi-class: Normal, DoS,
    Fuzzy, Gear, RPM
end note

note left of GW_ECU
  **Hardware examples:**
  Infineon AURIX TC3xx
  NXP S32G (Gateway)
  RAM: 256 KB – 4 MB
  Flash: 2 MB – 16 MB
end note

@enduml